.cpcache/
target/
node_modules/
.nrepl-port

# nbb's resolved-dependency cache. Ignoring this is safe HERE and the reason is
# measured, not assumed: nbb shells out to `bb` to build nbb-deps.jar, so a
# "cold cache + no bb" machine fails (exit 1, `bb: command not found`) — see
# docs/operator-quickstart.md §0. That only breaks CI if some CI runs nbb here,
# and none does: this repo has no .github/workflows and no fleet gate in
# scripts/fleet-ci/gates.edn targets it (checked 2026-09-10; the two `inkan`
# hits there are comments about a downstream consumer, isic-6910).
# If that ever changes, this line is the thing to revisit.
.nbb/
